.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL" "3JS" "August 7, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel \- LanguageModel
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]LanguageModel\f[B]\f[R] interface of the Prompt API
represents a session with a browser\-provided language model.
It exposes static methods for creating sessions and checking
availability, as well as instance methods for prompting the model,
appending context, and managing the context window.
.PP
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] instances cannot be constructed directly.
Instead, use the static \f[CR]LanguageModel.create()\f[R] method.
.SH STATIC METHODS
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.availability()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an enumerated value
indicating whether the language model is available for the given
options.
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.create()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with a new
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] session, downloading the model data if
necessary.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.append()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when the given input has been
added to the session\(cqs context window, without generating a response.
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.clone()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with a new
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] session that is a copy of the session it is
called on, including all context.
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.destroy()\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
Releases the resources assigned to the \f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] instance
it is called on and stops any further activity on it.
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.measureContextUsage()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with the number of context
window tokens that the given input would consume if it were used in an
operation such as \f[CR]prompt()\f[R] or \f[CR]append()\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.prompt()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with the model\(cqs complete
response to the given input.
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.promptStreaming()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] that streams the model\(cqs response
to the given input as it is generated.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.contextUsage\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns the number of context window tokens currently consumed by this
session.
.TP
\f[B]LanguageModel.contextWindow\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns the total context window size available for this session, in
tokens.
.SH EVENTS
.TP
\f[B]contextoverflow\f[R]
Fired when a \f[CR]prompt()\f[R], \f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R], or
\f[CR]append()\f[R] call exceeds the context window size.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Creating a session and prompting the model
This example first calls \f[CR]create()\f[R] to get a new session.
It specifies that the language model adopt a \f[CR]\(dqsystem\(dq\f[R]
role and defines how it should behave.
Note that the example uses \f[CR]await\f[R] because \f[CR]create()\f[R]
returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R].
This may take some time to resolve if the model needs to be downloaded.
.PP
After creating the session, the example calls \f[CR]prompt()\f[R] to ask
a specific question.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create({
  initialPrompts: [
    {
      role: \(dqsystem\(dq,
      content: \(dqYou are a helpful assistant.\(dq,
    },
  ],
});

\f[B]const\f[R] response = \f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt(\(dqWhat is the capital of France?\(dq);
console.log(response); \f[I]// \(dqThe capital of France is Paris.\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Streaming a response
This example calls \f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R] to get an instance of
\f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] and writes it to the console in chunks.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();
\f[B]const\f[R] readableStream = session.promptStreaming(\(dqTell me a short story.\(dq);

\f[B]for\f[R] \f[B]await\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] chunk \f[B]of\f[R] readableStream) {
  console.log(chunk);
}
.EE
